A||||4||Brucepts||Ugh the sunroof still leaks, help?||||1||
Z||000000||Brucepts||05-25-2001||09:32 PM||||Ok I've read all, well almost all the archives on this subject but was unable to find the answer to this question. The metal seal retainers (gutter?) on my sunroof seal are almost rusted away. Can they be replaced are they part of the roof? I didn't want to pull the seal out to findout and if they can't be replaced whats the fix for them? Also, I know you drill drain holes in the corners, but where and on what part do you drill the holes? Anyone have a detailed pic they could post? I don't want a hole down into the frame  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> All these questions pertain to an 84 SE. Thanks in advance . . .<P>------------------<BR>Advanced Dealer in the Great Material Continuum . . .||||reg||1
Z||000001||cadaver||05-26-2001||12:20 AM||||The holes go in the corners by the rubber seal. Down through the fiberglass. I think the factory holes in the later ones are 1/4. I drilled 1/2. If you still need a pic email me and I will send you one. I dont know about swapping out the frame. I dont remember how it is held in.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||05-26-2001||12:22 AM||||The channels that the weatherstrip fits into can be replaced -- they are simply pop rivetted in place.  There are 4 separate pieces.  Where you can get them is another matter.  I found the pieces that I needed on a junker that looked like it had hit a brick wall head on at 100 mph.  Everything from the front bumper thru the doors was smashed or bent (couldn't open the doors, steering wheel was pushed back towards the drive and the roof was folded).  I did drill the rivets out of these pieces and was able to get what I needed.  Had to straighten them out and then I just pop rivetted them into place on my sunroof panel.  <P>If you can't find what you need at a local boneyard, you might try the Mall Forum and see if someone can provide you with replacements.  <P>So far as drilling holes goes, I'm not exactly sure where the factory drilled them but I drilled a 1/4" hole in each corner towards the outer edge of the area that the weatherstip sites in.  You only want to drill thru the fiberglass (or whatever it is) roof skin.  You will know immediately when you have gone thru the skin -- STOP!!<P>There is a recent thread that talks about where and how to drill the holes.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierohoho||05-26-2001||03:23 PM||||Brucepts, check the thread from 05-22-01 titled Replacing Sunroff Weatherstrip.||||reg||1
